        "title": "6. Data Types",
        "body": "Values have **types** that decide what they are and what you can do with them.\n\n## The core types\n- **Integers** — whole numbers: `42`, `-7`.\n- **Floats / doubles** — decimals: `3.14`.\n- **Strings** — text: `\"hello\"`.\n- **Booleans** — `true` / `false`.\n- **Null / nil / None** — the absence of a value.\n- **Collections** — lists/arrays and key–value maps (covered later).\n\n## Static vs dynamic typing\nSome languages check types at compile time (catching mistakes early); others figure them out at runtime (more flexible, fewer guarantees). Neither is 'better' — they're different trade-offs.\n\n## Type errors\nMixing types incorrectly — like adding a number to text — is one of the most common beginner bugs. The error message usually tells you exactly which line.",
