        "body": "A **boolean** is a value that's either `true` or `false`, and it's the foundation of every decision a program makes.\n\n## Comparison operators\n`>` greater, `<` less, `>=`, `<=`, `==` equal, `!=` not equal. Each yields a boolean.\n\n## Combining conditions\n- **AND** — true only if both sides are true.\n- **OR** — true if either side is true.\n- **NOT** — flips true/false.\n\n## Watch out\n- `=` (assignment) vs `==` (comparison) is a classic bug.\n- Comparing floating-point numbers for exact equality is unreliable — compare with a small tolerance instead.",
