        "body": "**Loops** repeat work so you don't copy-paste.\n\n## The for loop\nWalk a counter through a range, running the body each step. Perfect when you know how many times to repeat.\n\n## Accumulators\nA classic pattern: start a `total = 0`, then add to it each pass. That's how you sum a range or a list.\n\n## Iterating collections\nMost languages let you loop directly over the items of a list/array (`for item in items`).\n\n## Common mistakes\n- **Off-by-one errors** — double-check whether your range is inclusive or exclusive of the end.\n- Modifying a collection while looping over it can cause surprises.",
